WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.609
Mobile Task Force operatives fire their assault
rifles at the approaching crowd of SCP-008

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:09.710
zombies, only to be swarmed and overwhelmed.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.440
Administrative staff try to activate the communications
arrays and contact help from another site,

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:20.890
but SCP-106 has melted all the wiring already,
keeping them cut off from the outside world.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:27.670
Able is drawing his obsidian blades to slice
and dice some unfortunate guards, and SCP-682

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:31.910
is running rampant in the halls, devouring
everyone he sees.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:37.570
In Site 19, thanks to the biggest containment
breach in modern records, the inmates are

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.550
now running the asylum.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.820
The guards are no longer in control, the researchers
have no information, and the administrative

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.260
staff is powerless.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.980
This time, the anomalies are on top.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.920
How will our heroes at the SCP Foundation
fare when the roles are all reversed?

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.859
First, we join Dr. Clef, the most trigger-happy
researcher that the SCP Foundation ever employed

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:04.979
- He never met an anomaly he didn’t propose
to terminate.

00:01:04.979 --> 00:01:09.060
Most of these anomalies, he’d be happy to
tell to their faces he wanted to terminate

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.060
them.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.650
This was a decision he may have wanted to
go back on now that the roles were reversed,

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.770
and he found himself strapped to a table with
a number of belts.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:21.842
He struggled against his restraints, but it
was no good.

00:01:21.842 --> 00:01:23.140
He was stuck tight.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.790
Standing above him was a D-Class possessed
by SCP-035, the Possessive Mask, carrying

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:30.869
one of Dr. Clef’s favorite shotguns.

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:36.460
A squad of cackling, vengeful members of D-Class
personnel stood behind him, egging him on.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.390
The Possessive Mask laughed and spoke.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:46.189
“Dr. Alto Clef, I have conferred with my
associates, the esteemed members of the SCP

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:47.189
Foundation’s D-Class personnel.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:55.990
And, in light of your poor conduct, belligerent
nature, and repeated acts of excessive aggression,

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.990
we think continued containment would present
undue risks.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.920
Instead, we recommend…

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.220
Immediate termination!”

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:09.599
Dr. Clef gulped, and the Possessive Mask cocked
his shotgun.

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:16.510
Elsewhere in the facility, SCP-076-1, Able,
the Immortal Warrior, was running some training

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:22.950
simulations - the exact kind that Mobile Task
Force operatives might run, but with a twist:

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:27.780
This time, it was Able’s training, and he
was using some captive Mobile Task Force officers

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.390
as training equipment.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.980
He’d taken away their guns and instead given
every single one of them one of his swords

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.710
- Which, it probably goes without saying,
they weren’t quite as adept with as he was.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.220
Not that Able cared.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.880
When he was ready to begin his “training
simulation”, he pulled out a blade in each

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:49.260
hand and jumped down into the training area.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:54.450
The sword-wielding MTF operatives were shaking
in their boots as he approached, the biggest,

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.580
most psychopathic smile stretched across his
face.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:01.659
The second that one of the MTF operatives
made the terrible mistake of raising his sword

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:05.989
and running in, Able effortlessly parried
him, and the slaughter began.

00:03:05.989 --> 00:03:11.140
By the time the “training simulation”
was done, Able was the only survivor.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:16.640
And none of the MTF Operatives would later
revive themselves in a giant, black sarcophagus.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.630
Meanwhile, SCP-682 was working on a more personal
project.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:26.860
One of the SCP Foundation’s most enduring
efforts was attempting to terminate SCP-682

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:32.770
at all costs, using some methods that even
hardcore sadists would describe as exceptionally

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:33.770
cruel.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:38.959
And the irreplaceable Dr. Jack Bright had
contributed more than his fair sure of potential

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:45.170
killing methods - Including using his anomalous
medallion to forcibly insert his consciousness

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:48.330
into 682’s own.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:54.690
But now that the roles were reversed, 682
wanted a little of that sweet, sweet payback.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:04:00.370
After devouring his fill of random researchers
and guards, 682 decided to narrow his focus

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:01.879
onto Dr. Bright.

00:04:01.879 --> 00:04:06.549
That’s exactly why he had Dr. Bright hanging
by his arms from a pair of chains above the

00:04:06.549 --> 00:04:11.360
same tank of acid that 682 had been wasting
away in for decades now.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:17.470
682 couldn’t wait for Dr. Bright to experience
the pain he’d known for so long.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:24.740
“Well, Doctor, we’ve tried burning, crushing,
and freezing, and still, it seems we can’t

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.580
give you a permanent death.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.160
We’ll try the acid now.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:35.780
I can tell you from personal experience, Doctor,
this acid is very, very effective.”

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:41.810
682 pulled a lever on the ground, loosening
the chains around Dr. Bright’s arms.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:47.250
As the wise-cracking researcher dropped down
towards the acid, 682 felt a profound sense

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.680
of calm.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.990
SCP-049, on the other hand, was feeling a
profound sense of excitement.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:58.699
After all, he’d spent months being experimented
on by low-level research staff, after having

00:04:58.699 --> 00:05:03.740
his own rights to research taken away after
a minor incident involving the death and subsequent

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.630
reanimation of Senior Researcher Hamlin.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:12.140
And now, with the tables turned and the roles
reversed, everything was about to change.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:17.979
049 had a whole gaggle of captured researchers
confined in a cell, the perfect testing stock

00:05:17.979 --> 00:05:21.600
for his next series of experiments into the
Pestilence.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:25.720
The Plague Doctor opened his bag and began
taking out each one of his frightening medical

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:32.091
tools, laying them across a nearby table and
ignoring the cries of protest from the cell.

00:05:32.091 --> 00:05:35.990
He feels no pity for them - They should be
honored to become part of such a towering

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.780
body of research.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:42.590
Their sacrifices would not be meaningless,
as their deaths would contribute to saving

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:44.530
so many other lives.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:49.740
The exact same logic that the SCP Foundation
uses to justify every piece of collateral

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.400
damage that they’ve ever incurred.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:56.090
But as the Plague Doctor walks towards the
cell with a scalpel, wondering which of the

00:05:56.090 --> 00:06:01.480
terrified researchers he’d select first,
none of them really appreciated the irony.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:08.110
Someone that did very much appreciate irony
was SCP-106, one of the most cruel, calculating,

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.850
and sadistic anomalies that the Foundation
has ever had to contain.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:16.620
While he wasn’t nearly as talkative as some
of the other sapient humanoid anomalies out

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.380
there, he was still extremely intelligent,
and he’d been observing the methods the

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.550
SCP Foundation had been using to contain him
for all these years.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:29.810
The one he found the most frustrating was
their tendency to make the area around his

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:34.850
containment cell extremely complicated, knowing
it would confuse him and make it that much

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:37.530
harder for him to escape.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:42.850
SCP-106 had been planning his particular method
of role reversal for years, and little by

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:46.750
little, building it in his beloved pocket
dimension.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:53.160
As soon as the anomalies took control of Site
19, SCP-106 captured a gaggle of researchers

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.470
and guards and dragged them to his hellish
pocket dimension.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:02.650
There, he trapped each one of them inside
cells in a twisted version of Site 19.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:07.650
As each one tried to escape, they found that
they were trapped in the same complex network

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:12.710
of obstacles that they’d always used to
keep SCP-106 contained.

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:17.750
The one difference is, in this case, they
were being chased by SCP-106.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:23.400
And they weren’t just playing for their
freedom, they were playing for their lives.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:28.479
It was the most fun SCP-106 had had in years.

00:07:28.479 --> 00:07:32.460
But not all of the anomalies subject to the
mass Site 19 role reversal were acting out

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.680
violent revenge fantasies.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:40.350
The anomalous butler, Mr. Deeds, summoned
up by the SCP-662 bell, was enjoying a real

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:43.110
change of pace under anomalous control.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:47.120
During the early hours of the containment
breach, a researcher had rung the bell and

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:50.110
summoned Mr. Deeds to help them control the
chaos.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:57.479
But, for some reason beyond anyone’s understanding,
Mr. Deeds had simply refused the orders.

00:07:57.479 --> 00:08:02.050
Not because they weren’t possible, as in
the case of his usual commands, but because

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.930
today, he simply didn’t feel like it.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:09.039
And if the Foundation personnel who summoned
him didn’t want him to alert more dangerous

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:13.520
anomalies of their presence, they needed to
wait on him for a change.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.360
It’s not like they had any choice in the
matter this time.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:21.260
That’s why Mr. Deeds was reclining in the
comfiest chair they could find, sipping on

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:26.180
a pina colada and getting a foot massage from
a nervous Junior Researcher.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:31.419
Even the anomaly who’d devoted his entire
life to service was, on this special day,

00:08:31.419 --> 00:08:36.669
deciding to take a load off and treat himself
to some much-needed rest and relaxation.

00:08:36.669 --> 00:08:39.090
And who could blame him, really?

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:43.510
SCP-1370, on the other hand, was choosing
to make war rather than love.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:48.930
Typically, this tiny, pathetic automaton known
as The Pesterbot was little more than an amusingly

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:52.339
useless sentient toy with delusions of grandeur.

00:08:52.339 --> 00:08:57.370
He wasn’t an anomaly that anyone took seriously,
and even fewer people feared him.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:03.590
In short, SCP-1370 was perhaps the biggest
loser in all of the Foundation’s containment.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:07.600
But now that the roles had been reversed,
he wasn’t so pathetic anymore.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.880
During the initial chaos of the containment
breach, while all the security personnel was

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.959
distracted by the significantly more dangerous
anomalies, the Pesterbot somehow managed to

00:09:16.959 --> 00:09:19.589
sneak his way into the experimental weapons
lab.

00:09:19.589 --> 00:09:24.690
That’s where he got his hands on a 40-watt
Phased Plasma rifle which promptly fused to

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:29.710
his little robot arm, allowing him to enact
a spree of chaotic shootings across his section

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.060
of the site.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:35.220
He cackled in his tinny robotic voice as guards
and researchers fled from him.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:40.560
He leveled his plasma rifle and fired glowing-hot
blasts in all directions, while declaring

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:44.560
himself to be the immutable mecha-lord of
all creation.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:48.440
And when he had such a deadly tool in his
hands - One that, with a single shot, could

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:54.070
superheat your skeleton into radioactive ash
- Nobody dared to dispute such a claim.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.839
Oh, how the tables had turned.

00:09:56.839 --> 00:09:59.910
But those weren’t the only researchers in
deep trouble.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:04.150
The grand role reversal had resulted in a
lot of researchers with less than ethical

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:08.470
scientific conduct getting a frightening taste
of their own medicine.

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:14.691
This is exactly what happened when a gang
of the infamous Laughing Men, SCP-2419, the

00:10:14.691 --> 00:10:19.650
vengeful bodies of soulless D-Class personnel,
managed to get their hands on the dog-bodied

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:23.130
senior researcher, Dr. Kain Pathos Crow.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:29.990
Dr. Crow had always been an aggressive user
of SCP-158, also known as the Soul Extractor.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:34.430
Using this machine, he had ripped out the
souls of many D-Classes as part of his frowned-upon

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:35.770
Olympia Project.

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:40.540
Naturally, this role reversal would not result
in Dr. Crow getting a favorable outcome.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:45.130
Instead, three Laughing Men forced him into
the Soul Extractor, which promptly removed

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.480
his soul and placed it into a jar.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:52.040
A jar which the Laughing Men then decided
to play a round of catch with.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:56.000
And honestly, as adorable as he may be, I
don’t think there’s any denying that Dr.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.760
Crow had this one coming.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.860
Maybe don’t extract so many people’s souls
next time, Doctor.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:05.600
But for some anomalies, the role reversal
was not a time for relaxation, rampaging,

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.050
or revenge.

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.830
It was a time for personal development.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:14.690
This was the case for SCP-2430, the Immortal
Hitler Clone.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.870
With all the chaos that was going on, the
daily staff Hitler-punching roster had fallen

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:24.320
by the wayside, allowing the anomalous ex-dictator
to leave his cell for once and wander around

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.320
the facility.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:30.570
Eventually, he found himself in a room he’d
never been in before: The Site 19 employee

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:35.380
library, which featured a wide range of both
anomalous and non-anomalous texts.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:40.320
This was where he found and decided, out of
sheer curiosity, to read a variety of personal

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:44.990
development and antiracism books that taught
him the error of his ways.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:50.339
For the first time, and in what was perhaps
the biggest role reversal of the entire breach,

00:11:50.339 --> 00:11:54.870
he began to realize that the philosophy of
discrimination he’d held in his previous

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:59.810
life had hurt hundreds of millions of people,
and put him on the road to nowhere.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:03.880
But before he could go any further down the
road of self-development, the long-awaited

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.590
cavalry arrived.

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:10.740
The fact that Site 19 had dropped out of contact
with other nearby sites for over ten hours

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:15.260
had raised alarm bells with the O5 Council,
who’d dispatched a wide array of Mobile

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:21.620
Task Forces to save the terrorized populace
of Site 19 and return Foundation control.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:26.589
All of the day’s role reversals were re-reversed
back into their original state.

00:12:26.589 --> 00:12:30.360
That’s right: Everything had been returned
to normal.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:31.360
For now, anyway…

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:35.300
Now go check out “Rick and Morty More Powerful
Than SCP Foundation?

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:41.410
Mad Scientist Battle!” and “SCP-343 God
Vs Bill Cipher From Gravity Falls” for more!

